      "gain_m": null,
      "descent_m": null,
      "description": "Another good run can be had from the north summit of Outlook Mountain (486200 E 5509800 N). Head north, then curve down to the right to reach Kokanee Pass (s50 vertical metres). The approach to this peak is up Outlook Creek to Lemon Pass, where the way above is blocked by a short steep section. It is possible to ascend the obstacle by a narrow crest just above Lemon Pass (485100 E 55113°0 N).",
      "notes": "Guide note: si3 'north summit of Outlook Mountain (486200 E 5509800 N)' coincides with today's Mount John Carter (ATES landmark within ~60 m). 's50 vertical metres' is a typo (likely 550 or 650). '55113°0' = 5511300; '55II300' = 5511300. Placement: from Mount John Carter summit (= the printed north summit of Outlook, lidar 2609 m) N along the crest, then right (NE) to Kokanee Pass taken as the DEM low point between Kokanee and Keen lakes (486805/5511705, 2026 m); the BCGNIS pass point sits 870 m S on a 46 deg slope, so it was not used. Vertical 583 m fits 's50' read as 550. Skin crosses Kaslo Lake, goes up Outlook Creek to the printed crest ref (485100/5511300, unreliable) and follows the ridge SE to the summit; the BCGNIS Lemon Pass is 900 m W and lower, so S&I's 'Lemon Pass' is assumed to be the col by Sapphire Lakes.",
